-    "lem-total-variation-coupling-and-kernel-contraction": {
-      "source_path": "items/lem-total-variation-coupling-and-kernel-contraction.md",
-      "kind": "lemma",
-      "status": "published",
-      "source_section": "Statement",
-      "excerpt": "Let $\\mu,\\nu$ be probability measures on $(\\mathsf X,\\mathcal X)$ and let\n$P$ be a probability kernel on that space. Then\n$$\\lVert\\mu-\\nu\\rVert_{\\rm TV}=\\sup_{f:\\mathsf X\\to[0,1]\\ \\mathcal X\\text{-measurable}}\\left|\\int f\\,d\\mu-\\int f\\,d\\nu\\right|,$$\n$$\\lVert\\mu P-\\nu P\\rVert_{\\rm TV}\\le\\lVert\\mu-\\nu\\rVert_{\\rm TV}.$$\nIf $(U,V)$ is a coupling of $\\mu$ and $\\nu$ on a probability space and\n$E$ is a measurable event on which $U=V$, then\n$$\\lVert\\mu-\\nu\\rVert_{\\rm TV}\\le\\mathbb P(E^c).$$",
