-    "thm-ionescu-tulcea-construction-of-a-markov-chain": {
-      "source_path": "items/thm-ionescu-tulcea-construction-of-a-markov-chain.md",
-      "kind": "theorem",
-      "status": "published",
-      "source_section": "Statement",
-      "excerpt": "Assume Choice. Let $(E_n,\\mathcal E_n)_{n\\ge0}$ be measurable spaces, let\n$\\mu_0$ be a probability measure on $E_0$, and, for each $n\\ge0$, let $K_n$ be\na probability kernel from $E_0\\times\\cdots\\times E_n$ to $E_{n+1}$. There is a\nunique probability measure $P$ on\n$$ \\left(\\prod_{n\\ge0}E_n,\\ \\bigotimes_{n\\ge0}\\mathcal E_n\\right) $$ whose finite-prefix laws are the prescribed iterated integrals $$ \\mu_0(dx_0)K_0(x_0,dx_1)K_1(x_0,x_1,dx_2)\\cdots K_{r-1}(x_0,\\ldots,x_{r-1},dx_r). $$\nIn particular, if every $E_n=E$ and\n$K_n(x_0,\\ldots,x_n,A)=K(x_n,A)$, the coordinate process is a homogeneous\n$K$-chain with initial law $\\mu_0$.",
-      "excerpt_sha256": "fed2a825628255c3666567dac04b590375054c3cd80f02209d66099e573bda04",
-      "readiness": {
-        "status": "published"
